The function is a plain getter, so there is little to gain inside its body. The change below is behavior-identical. The real cost is the out-of-line call, and moving the definition into the header as `inline` would fix that, but the rules keep this to one function body.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Mesg::GetLocalNum() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 n = localNum;
    return n;
}
```